{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JER",
  "chapter": 5,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JER.5.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Run ye to and fro through the streets of Jerusalem, and see now, and know, and seek in its broad places, if ye can find a man, if there is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that executeth judgment, that seeketh the truth; and I will pardon it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And though they say, The LORD liveth; surely they swear falsely.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not thy eyes upon the truth? thou hast stricken them, but they have not grieved; thou hast consumed them, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they have refused to receive correction: they have made their faces harder than a rock; they have refused to return.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I said, Surely these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " poor; they are foolish: for they know not the way of the LORD, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "nor",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the judgment of their God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will go to the great men, and will speak to them; for they have known the way of the LORD, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the judgment of their God: but these have altogether broken the yoke, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " burst the bonds.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore a lion from the forest shall slay them, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a wolf of the evenings shall spoil them, a leopard shall watch over their cities: every one that goeth out thence shall be torn in pieces: because their transgressions are many, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their backslidings are increased.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How shall I pardon thee for this? thy children have forsaken me, and sworn by ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them that are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no gods: when I had fed them to the full, then they committed adultery, and assembled themselves by troops in the harlots' houses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They were ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fed horses in the morning: every one neighed after his neighbor's wife.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall I not visit for these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "? saith the LORD: and shall not my soul be avenged on such a nation as this?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Go ye up upon her walls, and destroy; but make not a full end: take away her battlements; for they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not the LORD'S.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the house of Israel and the house of Judah have dealt very treacherously against me, saith the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have belied the LORD, and said, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not he; neither shall evil come upon us; neither shall we see sword nor famine:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the prophets shall become wind, and the word ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not in them: thus shall it be done to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore thus saith the LORD God of hosts, Because ye speak this word, Behold, I will make my words in thy mouth fire, and this people wood, and it shall devour them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo, I will bring a nation upon you from far, O house of Israel, saith the LORD: it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a mighty nation, it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an ancient nation, a nation whose language thou knowest not, neither understandest what they say.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their quiver ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as an open sepulcher, they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all mighty men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they shall eat up thy harvest, and thy bread, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy sons and thy daughters should eat: they shall eat up thy flocks and thy herds: they shall eat up thy vines and thy fig-trees: they shall impoverish with the sword thy fortified cities, in which thou hast trusted.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless in those days, saith the LORD, I will not make a full end with you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it shall come to pass, when ye shall say, Why doeth the LORD our God all these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to us? then shalt thou answer them, As ye have forsaken me, and served strange gods in your land, so shall ye serve strangers in a land ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not yours.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Declare this in the house of Jacob, and publish it in Judah, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear now this, O foolish people, and without understanding; who have eyes, and see not; who have ears, and hear not:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fear ye not me? saith the LORD: will ye not tremble at my presence, who have placed the sand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the bound of the sea by a perpetual decree, that it cannot pass it: and though its waves toss themselves, yet can they not prevail; though they roar, yet can they not pass over it?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But this people have a revolting and a rebellious heart; they have revolted and gone.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Neither say they in their heart, Let us now fear the LORD our God, that giveth rain, both the former and the latter, in its season: he reserveth to us the appointed weeks of harvest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Your iniquities have turned away these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and your sins have withheld good ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For among my people are found wicked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": they lay wait, as he that setteth snares; they set a trap, they catch men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As a cage is full of birds, so ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their houses full of deceit: therefore they have become great, and have grown rich.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have become fat, they shine: yes, they surpass the deeds of the wicked: they judge not the cause, the cause of the fatherless, yet they prosper; and the right of the needy do they not judge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall I not visit for these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "? saith the LORD: shall not my soul be avenged on such a nation as this?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A wonderful and horrible thing is committed in the land;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.5.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.5.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The prophets prophesy falsely, and the priests bear rule by their means; and my people love ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to have it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " so: and what will ye do in the end thereof?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
